  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on variance — a measure of dispersion — and prefers the higher-variance option (Lottery B). However, the individual’s deliberation centers on the probability of winning and the security of a positive outcome, explicitly favoring certainty. They do not consider or mention any statistical measure of spread or variability. Their justification is aligned with risk aversion, not variance maximization. In fact, they choose the option with lower variance (A), which contradicts the rule of the decision reason. The information considered (probability of non-zero gain, amount size) and the justification (certainty over uncertainty) do not align with the variance-based reason. Therefore, it is certain that the individual did not use the variance-maximizing reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
